## 3. PORTFOLIO CONSTRUCTION & RISK MANAGEMENT

### 3.1 Portfolio Architecture

PNP operated as a **massive collection of isolated, market-neutral hedges**:

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph Individual Hedge
        LONG[LONG undervalued asset]
        SHORT[SHORT overvalued asset]
    end
    Individual Hedge --> LLN[Law of Large Numbers × hundreds of hedges]
    LLN --> Result[Result: Bond-like vol less than Equity-like returns]
```

### 3.2 Capital Allocation Framework

| Priority | Strategy | Rationale |
|----------|----------|-----------|
| 1 | Short-dated warrants (<4yr expiry) | Fastest convergence → highest annualized return |
| 2 | Convertible arbitrage | Same hedging mechanics, different instrument |
| 3 | OTC options | Nascent market, less competition |
| 4 | Index arbitrage | Later iteration, lower margins |
| 5 | Pairs trading | Ongoing statistical opportunities |

**Allocation rule:** When strategies appear equal, split capital (e.g., 40/40/20 across three targets) to maximize diversification.

### 3.3 Drawdown Management

**Built-in Kelly Safeguards:**
- Losing streak → capital shrinks → absolute dollar bet shrinks (automatic safety brake)
- Winning streak → capital grows → absolute dollar bet expands (automatic compounding)
- **NEVER** increase bet size to "win back" losses — this violates Kelly math and guarantees ruin

**Structural Protection:**
- Every trade is a hedged pair — market crashes don't affect the spread
- Zero-profit-line mapping ensures downside is mathematically bounded
- Maximum practical leverage capped at **2.0×** (50% margin)

### 3.4 Rebalancing

**Approach:** Trigger-based, not calendar-based
- Execute rebalance ONLY if expected growth increase > transaction cost
- For short positions: use **Avalanche Effect** — as price drops, released margin funds additional shorts without new cash
- No cookie-cutter daily/weekly schedule

### 3.5 Liquidity & Capacity Management

| Constraint | Solution |
|------------|----------|
| Short borrow availability | Multiple brokerages, diversify borrow sources |
| Short sale up-tick rule | Park released capital in short-term bonds until executable |
| Position size limits | Spread across accounts, use same-day substitution |
| Capital efficiency | Reg T §220.3(g) same-day substitution maximizes velocity |

